New York Attorney General Eric  Schneiderman is not the new york stock  exchange in these joining me now  attorney general thank you for being  here talk to me first about exactly how  this is going to get structured 800  million of the roughly 17 billion  dollars worth of fines is going to go to  New York yes we were getting 300 million  in cash but we have a minimum of 500  million in consumer relief and the  consumer relief that's being offered in  the bank of america settlement is really  much it's a much broader set of menu  items than there was any there were  neither the chase or the city deals and  we expect in New York to do much better  than the 500 million which the bank is  obliged to provide us and we've done  better in previous settlements when they  did the first national mortgage  servicing settlement HUD estimated that  New York families would get about six  hundred million dollars worth of  principal reduction and other relief we  got over two billion dollars because  we've set up what I think is the best  network in the country of legal services  and housing counselors to help people  who are eligible for programs know what  programs they're eligible for you  mentioned legal services and and  counseling programs for housing I mean  one of the fears here attorney  Schneiderman is that all this money gets  paid to the government and it doesn't  actually get back to the people who need  it most or who may have been victims  from this kind of fraud what actually  happens to it in terms of the consumers  that might need it will they see  anything sure the consumers are saying  it the the network of legal services and  housing counselors is set up because  these are people who know what consumers  are eligible for if I'm an average  homeowner there may be a federal  modification program available there may  be a bank modification program I won't  know about it it's hard to tell these  legal services and housing counseling  folks over 90 agencies around the state  are they've already helped more than  30,000 New York families figure out what  they were eligible for and they provide  legitimate advice I have to say there  also is the sub industry of scammers who  are pretending they will help New  Yorkers and others in other parts of the  country get their mortgages redone we're  getting people's mortgages written down  principal reductions rate reductions all  over the state of New York and this  money just started flowing in the last  year or so you're going to see a lot of  relief to a lot of homeowners and in  state of New York we're not just dealing  with individual homeowners were also  funding land banks to help communities  where you have a lot of abandoned  properties that bring down the property  values ruin the tax base we're helping  the people who were really hit by the  crash has sort of collateral damage they  didn't get foreclosed on themselves but  because their communities were  devastated their suffering too so this  is a comprehensive approach and in our  office we have an open request for  proposal process and rfp process for any  money we give at is all posted on our  website so the money is not sticking in  some government bureaucracy there's been  no criminal prosecution to speak of do  you regret that um I think that if  things had gotten started a little bit  earlier there might have been some  criminal cases to be made i think that  when i came in in january 2011 as the  tourney generalist started to get a  sense of what the scope of this problem  was we did the best we could i'm proud  of the fact that we fought to establish  the working group that the president set  up in january 2012 and the chase steal  the city deal and this record-breaking  deal with Bank of America are all coming  out of the work of this national working  group the President Obama set up in  January 2012 he doesn't get mentioned a  lot in these stories but he's the one  who put justice in my office and the SEC  and others together and we really  started ramping up the cases in DOJ  putting more resources and that's why  we're getting these record-breaking  attorney Sneiderman what do you say to  those who critique this and say you know  what bank of america really helped the  country at a time when it needed help  because countrywide and merrill lynch  were acquired by bank of america and as  a result a lot of the pain and suffering  that could have come with both of those  banks going under did not happen what do  you say in response to this to say this  really isn't fair because this is coming  back to hurt them in the end at a time  when they were trying to help look these  are not charitable organizations I have  very high regard for the management  bank of america city and chase but they  made deals they thought were in their  financial interest when JP Morgan took  over Bear Stearns they were touting it  as one of the great steals of the  century it appeared to be a great deal  same thing with countrywide and bank of  america and at the end of the day these  institutions all got bailed out by the  federal government they paid back the  money but there were no strings attached  to the bailout so there was no  additional benefit the American people I  think the financial institutions did  what they had to do they're out to make  money fair enough if I buy stock in one  of these companies I want them to try  and make money for me but I don't want  them to engage in the kind of reckless  misconduct that brought the economy to  its knees but they didn't make money in  these particular cases they lost money  on all of these and then they got bailed  out and they're back in there back in  the black how many more fines do you  anticipate coming forward I mean are we  nearing the end of this cycle now with  this record-breaking nearly 17 billion  dollars well the total that we've  recovered in cash a consumer relief if  you count the chase city bank of america  and the national mortgage servicing  settlement we're up over sixty billion  dollars in cash and consumer relief as a  result of these collective efforts there  there are more institutions out there  and i'm looking forward to this and i do  have to say i think that the management  of JPMorgan Chase city in bank of  america history will look back and say  it was a smart move to get all this  behind you it all of the deals on the  table gather up every agency every state  AG that he might have a case with put it  behind you there's a piece premium for  all the banks that do the right thing  and settle and I'm glad we were able to  work this out at the bank of america  before I let you go I know you've been  looking very significantly into high  frequency trading any updates on your  hft investigations that you can share  with us right now not that I can share  with you right now but there was a  motion filed in the Barclays case that  we will be responding to early next  month okay we're gonna leave it there  thank you very much for joining me here  today from the New York Stock Exchange  Attorney General of New York Eric  Schneiderman

